<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nebuchadnezzar I</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar</a> I was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> in the late twelfth century BCE, of the Second Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isin">Isin</a>. After the Elamite overthrow of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassite-dynasty">Kassite dynasty</a>, he led a Babylonian revival. He is best known for his campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> that recovered the statue of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marduk">Marduk</a>, a blow recorded in the history of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-i.jpg" alt="Nebuchadnezzar I" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osama Shukir Muhammed Amin FRCP(Glasg) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Detail,_Kudurru_of_Ritti-Marduk,_from_Sippar,_Iraq,_1125-1104_BCE._British_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
